{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"runesleo-systematic-debugging","displayName":"Systematic Debugging","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/runesleo/skills/runesleo-systematic-debugging","publisherHandle":"runesleo","publisherDisplayName":"runesleo","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/runesleo","version":"3.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772890916061,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/runesleo-systematic-debugging/card?ownerHandle=runesleo&version=3.0.0","sha256":"6696ae06dc50f7c40678a67b357f26351dafd0989c3f630b5adf5444f7100c68","size":1739,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"0f485f9c82ad4656ca2a18d4094f09c938e4ebefff09118670c2bb5076220957","bundleFingerprints":["1d8fcd5b5d9933509bd98dddd83767843a319680e40167bea879258639750261","d9e954b3765418e36103ae66fcadba333ea095607a56747e03d7c6173296f73a"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9006,"sha256":"3ee7742b20dd0a2a935c46d65424cb8495b60020b8cad0fae3172933c05007bd","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a normal debugging guide, but it directs agents to check memory files or past conversations before debugging, which can expose unrelated sensitive history.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789112194552,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T05","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Mandatory Access to Agent Memory and Past Conversations"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":55,"endLine":72}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"65cd2ccd11c9576e"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 55–72  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Excessive access to cross-session memory and conversation data  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```markdown\n### Phase 0: Context Recall (MANDATORY FIRST STEP)\n\n**BEFORE doing ANYTHING else:**\n\n1. **Extract Keywords from Error**\n   - What's the error type? (OOM, timeout, connection, type error...)\n   - What component? (server, browser, API, database...)\n   - What area of the codebase?\n\n2. **Search for Prior Knowledge**\n   - Check project docs, MEMORY files, or past conversations\n   - Search codebase for similar error patterns: `grep -r \"ErrorType\" .`\n   - Check git log for related recent changes: `git log --oneline -20`\n\n3. **Review Results**\n   - Found relevant experience? -> **Apply directly, skip to Phase 4**\n   - Found partial match? -> Use as starting point for Phase 1\n   - Nothing found? -> Proceed to Phase 1, **remember to record solution later**\n\n4. **Output Format**\n   ```\n   Context Recall:\n   - Query: \"xxx\"\n   - Found: [description of related knowledge]\n   - Action: [apply experience / continue investigation / no match]\n   ```\n\n**VIOLATION:** Proceeding to Phase 1 without Context Recall output = process failure.\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe Skill makes context recall mandatory before any debugging activity and explicitly directs the agent to inspect `MEMORY` files or past conversations. These sources can contain credentials, personal information, confidential project details, or data belonging to unrelated users and tasks.\n\nThis instruction violates least-privilege principles because routine debugging generally requires only the current error, relevant source files, tests, project documentation, and version history. It provides no consent requirement, relevance boundary, access restriction, or redaction procedure. The required context-recall output may also cause information discovered in those sources to be reproduced in the active conversation.\n\nThe instruction to apply recalled experience directly and skip to Phase 4 further reduces opportunities to validate whether recalled material belongs to the current project or remains safe and accurate.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. The Skill activates for a bug, test failure, or other technical issue.\n2. Phase 0 requires context recall before the agent performs any other debugging activity.\n3. The agent searches available `MEMORY` files or past conversations.\n4. Sensitive or unrelated cross-session information is loaded into the active context.\n5. The mandatory context-recall summary may disclose details from that information in the current conversation.\n6. Recalled instructions or solutions may be applied directly without a complete current-project investigation.\n\nNo external transmission mechanism or persistent privilege escalation was identified in the audited file.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe accessible scope depends on the host agent's permissions. If the agent can read persistent memory or prior conversation history, the instruction may expose any sensitive information stored there to the current session. Potentially affected data includes credentials, personal data, confidential source-code context, and information from unrelated tasks or users.\n\nThe finding does not provide operating-system privilege escalation, code execution, persistence, or remote exfiltration by itself. Its primary impact is unnecessary cross-session data access and possible disclosure through generated output.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove the unconditional instruction to inspect `MEMORY` files and past conversations.\n2. Restrict default context discovery to the current project, including its errors, documentation, source code, tests, and version history.\n3. Require explicit user authorization before accessing persistent memory or cross-session conversation data.\n4. Apply strict relevance and tenant boundaries so the agent cannot access information belonging to unrelated users, projects, or tasks.\n5. Add redaction controls that prevent credentials, tokens, personal data, and confidential content from appearing in context-recall output.\n6. Replace direct reuse of recalled solutions with a validation step against the current codebase and environment.\n7. Revise the instruction as follows:\n\n```markdown\nSearch the current project's documentation, source code, tests, and version\nhistory for relevant prior knowledge. Access persistent memory or past\nconversations only when the user explicitly authorizes it and the data is\nscoped to the current project. Never reproduce secrets or unrelated content\nin the context-recall summary.\n```"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789112117.456492,"endTime":1789112161.5288835}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"Systematic Debugging","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v570m4khm5tjds3j8k5d17cm2d8e76s4-q4EesY/clawscan-skillspector-3765561311/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T07:35:16.493562+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"NONE"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":270,"executable":false,"size_bytes":9006,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":false,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4281,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4295},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4354,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4368},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3886,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3900}],"filtering_mode":"heuristic","llm_calls_attempted":3,"llm_calls_succeeded":3},"execution_successful":true,"analysis_completeness":{"total_components":1,"scanned_components":1,"coverage_percent":100,"is_complete":false,"status":"partial","execution_successful":true,"fully_inspected_files":1,"partially_inspected_files":0,"entirely_uninspected_files":0,"ledger_exceptions":[{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7,"fatal":false},{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":118,"end_line":118,"fatal":false},{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":211,"end_line":211,"fatal":false}],"scope_exclusions":[],"analyzer_statuses":[{"analyzer_id":"artifact_integrity","status":"completed","planned_work":1,"completed":1,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0},{"analyzer_id":"behavioral_ast","status":"not_applicable","planned_work":0,"completed":0,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0,"reason_code":"no_applicable_files","message":"No files matched this analyzer's appli